  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive Approach to Integrated and Accessible Mental Health in Georgia (COMPASS - GE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;Overall Objective: To comprehensively strenghten mental healthcare system in Georgia by rights-based, evidence-informed policies and practices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;em&gt;Specific objective(s) &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.To analyse and update the national mental health (MH) legislation and policy, based on current knowldege and local evidence on mental health needs and systematic gaps in Georgian MH system;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2.To strengthen capacities of key stakeholders, among them mental health specialists and persons with lived experience, with rights-based approaches across prevention, treatment &amp; management and recovery domains of MH care;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;To conduct inclusive policy dialogues and advocate for adoption of rights-based, integrated and accessible policies and practices in MH care;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;To contribute to mental health literacy and awareness raising through mental health promotional events and campaigning across the country.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
